EXT. MOONLIT CLEARING - THE WHISPERING WOOD - NIGHT

A ring of white birches. Pale mushrooms glow along the roots. A stream runs backwards through the grass, climbing a low hill and disappearing into the trees. The air hums like a plucked string.

Six travellers stand within the ring.

BRIAR THORNWICK (40s, dwarf cartographer, spectacles, a coat of many pockets) unrolls a map and weighs its corners with pebbles. LYSANDRA (20s, elven archer, silver braid, a quiver slung low) stands on one foot, listening. FINN OSRIC (teen, farm boy, borrowed sword too large for him) hugs his elbows. SISTER MERIWEN (50s, wandering priestess, grey robe, knotted staff) kneels and touches the backwards stream. GRIMBLE (age unknown, gnome tinkerer, goggles pushed up on his forehead) pokes at a mushroom with a spoon.

BRIAR
We are here.

He puts a finger on the map. Lysandra glances over his shoulder.

LYSANDRA
That is not here. That is a lake.

BRIAR
The map says lake.

LYSANDRA
The map is old.

SISTER MERIWEN
The stream runs uphill. Which is odd, even for this wood.

FINN
Is it magic?

SISTER MERIWEN
It's something.

GRIMBLE
It's glowing. Look! The mushrooms are humming!

Grimble holds the spoon up. A fat orange mushroom hums a low C. Finn laughs, nervous.

Between two birches, a pale shape detaches itself from the dark. A woman in a gown of cobweb and moonlight, hair long as a river, feet not quite touching the ground. This is the WARDEN OF THE WOOD (ageless, solemn). She regards them.

WARDEN
You are far from the road.

BRIAR
We have a map.

WARDEN
Your map is a lie the trees agreed to tell.

Briar closes the map. Lysandra draws an arrow and lets it hang, unnocked. Finn's sword droops. Meriwen rises, bowing her head.

SISTER MERIWEN
We seek passage to the Southern Keep.

WARDEN
Passage costs a song.

GRIMBLE
I know one! Do you want the one about the frog?

WARDEN
I want the truest song you know.

All of them are quiet. Finn hesitates, steps forward, and begins to sing, small and out of tune, a farm song his mother taught him.
